{
  "_why": "One source for the semantic colours; scripts/check-palette.py generates src/palette.css from it and verifies it: WCAG 2.1 contrast in both themes and both colour sets. Neutrals are true greys with dark-grey text (about 12:1 for body text, readable without the glare of black on white); navy is the one brand accent. Status colours come in two sets, chosen per reader in Settings: 'light'/'dark' carry the conventional green, amber and red, which must differ by at least dE 20 under normal vision; 'friendly' replaces them with colours that stay at least dE 20 apart under normal, protan, deutan and tritan vision too (Machado et al. 2009). Teal, green and rust accents were rejected: they merge with success for red-green colour-blind readers. Info reuses the brand blue: a second blue merged with green under tritan vision.",
